    "description": "The Igloo ICEB26 is the cheap, fast way to make ice for a cooler, a dorm or an RV. Walmart and Kohl's list output of 26 lb per 24 hours with nine bullet-shaped cubes in as little as seven minutes, a choice of cube sizes and an automatic self-cleaning cycle with a drain plug. Listings disagree on tank size (2 quarts at Walmart versus 3 quarts at Kohl's) and basket capacity (1.25 lb versus 2 lb), so check the exact model suffix. Bullet ice is hollow and melts faster than nugget or cube ice, and the basket is not a freezer, so ice slowly melts back into the reservoir to be refrozen. That is normal for this class. It typically sells near the $100 mark, far below nugget machines.",
